WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:11.131
The next day, back in shelf.

2
00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:15.299
imece opens where you left off.

3
00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:18.831
The old reply can go: r dismisses it.

4
00:00:32.242 --> 00:00:36.286
Colon lonca import puts the project on Lonca.

5
00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:43.835
From now on, workers work in Lonca workspaces, and Lonca keeps them from editing the

6
00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:44.733
same code.

7
00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:51.646
Now a bigger task, for a team: lending, split so that two workers can work at once.

8
00:01:07.137 --> 00:01:14.277
Before a second worker, the leader shows you its plan: the cards, which files each

9
00:01:14.277 --> 00:01:17.237
one owns, and what it should cost.

10
00:01:17.237 --> 00:01:19.588
W opens it, enter reads it.

11
00:01:27.338 --> 00:01:28.909
A says yes.

12
00:01:34.239 --> 00:01:38.450
Two workers start, each in a workspace of its own.

13
00:01:43.741 --> 00:01:46.046
Colon code shows who edits what.

14
00:01:46.046 --> 00:01:51.736
Each worker holds a lease on the files and functions it changes, so nobody else

15
00:01:51.736 --> 00:01:53.392
touches them meanwhile.

16
00:02:09.743 --> 00:02:11.886
Both changes wait for you.

17
00:02:11.886 --> 00:02:18.563
After your yes, Lonca runs the tests on the merged result, and only then does the

18
00:02:18.563 --> 00:02:20.294
change land on trunk.

19
00:02:20.294 --> 00:02:26.394
The second one was based on the old trunk: Lonca merges it after your yes.

20
00:02:33.845 --> 00:02:37.696
The journal tells the story, card by card.

21
00:02:41.647 --> 00:02:44.869
Colon sync brings trunk into your checkout.

22
00:02:44.869 --> 00:02:49.738
Bang runs a command in your own shell: all twenty-six tests pass.

23
00:03:11.148 --> 00:03:13.439
That is a team, on Lonca.

24
00:03:16.049 --> 00:03:20.781
The guide has every key and command, and a one-page cheat sheet.

